WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.327
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online C one, Book four.

2
00:00:05.627 --> 00:00:08.944
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.244 --> 00:00:16.703
Unit twenty-two: Human Resource Management. Today you will state workplace requirements with it is essential that + subjunctive.

4
00:00:17.003 --> 00:00:19.632
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.567 --> 00:00:24.241
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.083 --> 00:00:26.084
Recruitment.

7
00:00:27.083 --> 00:00:30.302
Recruitment means the process of finding and hiring employees.

8
00:00:30.917 --> 00:00:33.950
Recruitment through universities brought in fresh talent.

9
00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:37.202
Your turn. Say: Recruitment.

10
00:00:40.067 --> 00:00:41.068
Recruitment.

11
00:00:41.817 --> 00:00:42.644
Talent.

12
00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:46.555
Talent means skilled people, or a natural ability.

13
00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:50.369
Competition for digital talent is fierce in Phnom Penh.

14
00:00:50.983 --> 00:00:53.380
Your turn. Say: Talent.

15
00:00:56.233 --> 00:00:57.130
Talent.

16
00:00:57.883 --> 00:00:58.583
Training.

17
00:00:59.583 --> 00:01:02.152
Training means teaching employees new skills.

18
00:01:02.750 --> 00:01:06.212
Monthly training improved customer satisfaction scores.

19
00:01:06.817 --> 00:01:09.167
Your turn. Say: Training.

20
00:01:12.033 --> 00:01:12.849
Training.

21
00:01:13.583 --> 00:01:14.619
Performance.

22
00:01:15.617 --> 00:01:18.417
Performance means how well someone does their job.

23
00:01:19.017 --> 00:01:21.434
Performance reviews take place twice a year.

24
00:01:22.050 --> 00:01:24.853
Your turn. Say: Performance.

25
00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:28.666
Performance.

26
00:01:29.417 --> 00:01:30.441
Retention.

27
00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:34.007
Retention means keeping employees from leaving.

28
00:01:34.617 --> 00:01:37.197
Flexible hours improved staff retention.

29
00:01:37.783 --> 00:01:40.807
Your turn. Say: Retention.

30
00:01:43.667 --> 00:01:44.726
Retention.

31
00:01:45.483 --> 00:01:46.287
Culture.

32
00:01:47.283 --> 00:01:50.897
Culture means the shared values and behaviour in an organisation.

33
00:01:51.483 --> 00:01:54.052
A culture of respect keeps good people.

34
00:01:54.650 --> 00:01:56.954
Your turn. Say: Culture.

35
00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:00.650
Culture.

36
00:02:01.417 --> 00:02:02.255
Wellbeing.

37
00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:07.154
Wellbeing means a state of being healthy, safe and content.

38
00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:10.794
The company introduced wellbeing days after Pchum Ben.

39
00:02:11.383 --> 00:02:13.722
Your turn. Say: Wellbeing.

40
00:02:16.567 --> 00:02:17.649
Wellbeing.

41
00:02:18.383 --> 00:02:19.442
Diversity.

42
00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:23.727
Diversity means including people of different backgrounds.

43
00:02:24.317 --> 00:02:27.245
Diversity in the team led to more creative ideas.

44
00:02:27.850 --> 00:02:30.375
Your turn. Say: Diversity.

45
00:02:33.233 --> 00:02:34.409
Diversity.

46
00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:39.048
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:39.883 --> 00:02:45.566
Visal, the hotel loses half its staff every year. The manager says young people just aren't loyal.

48
00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:55.609
I disagree. Exit interviews show staff leave because of unfair shifts. It is essential that every employee be treated fairly.

49
00:02:56.717 --> 00:02:58.890
But the hotel pays above the market rate.

50
00:02:59.983 --> 00:03:09.102
Pay matters, but it isn't enough. It is vital that managers recognise good work and that schedules be published in advance.

51
00:03:10.217 --> 00:03:12.042
So what would you recommend?

52
00:03:13.150 --> 00:03:21.642
Training for supervisors and a clear career path. It is crucial that staff see a future in the company, not just a job.

53
00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:24.428
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:25.283 --> 00:03:28.537
Grammar focus: It is essential that plus subjunctive.

55
00:03:28.837 --> 00:03:29.989
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:30.683 --> 00:03:33.786
It is essential that every employee be treated fairly.

57
00:03:34.683 --> 00:03:38.041
It is vital that each new worker receive proper training.

58
00:03:38.950 --> 00:03:41.878
It is crucial that staff see a future in the company.

59
00:03:42.833 --> 00:03:56.225
In formal English, adjectives like essential, vital, crucial and important are followed by 'that + subject + base verb' (the subjunctive): that he be, that she receive (no -s). British English also allows 'should': that he should be.

60
00:03:56.983 --> 00:04:00.901
Be careful! Don't say: It is essential that he is on time.

61
00:04:02.867 --> 00:04:05.458
Say: It is essential that he be on time.

62
00:04:05.758 --> 00:04:07.537
Subjunctive: base verb.

63
00:04:08.333 --> 00:04:11.125
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:11.933 --> 00:04:13.492
People Are the Strategy.

65
00:04:13.792 --> 00:04:20.795
Human resource management covers the entire employee journey, from recruitment and training to performance management and retention.

66
00:04:21.800 --> 00:04:28.676
Research consistently shows that people leave managers, not companies, so it is essential that supervisors be trained in leadership.

67
00:04:29.667 --> 00:04:35.393
Replacing an employee can cost up to a year's salary once recruitment and lost productivity are included.

68
00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:41.883
Modern HR therefore focuses on culture, wellbeing and diversity as well as pay.

69
00:04:42.867 --> 00:04:50.149
In Cambodia's competitive labour market, firms that invest in their people increasingly outperform those that treat staff as a cost.

70
00:04:51.233 --> 00:04:55.432
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:56.283 --> 00:04:58.608
It is essential that she blank on time.

72
00:04:58.908 --> 00:05:02.085
A, is. B, be. C, will be.

73
00:05:05.633 --> 00:05:07.192
The answer is B: be.

74
00:05:08.350 --> 00:05:10.675
Keeping employees from leaving is blank.

75
00:05:10.975 --> 00:05:14.686
A, retention. B, recruitment. C, diversity.

76
00:05:18.233 --> 00:05:20.059
The answer is A: retention.

77
00:05:21.217 --> 00:05:24.133
A state of being healthy, safe and content is blank.

78
00:05:24.433 --> 00:05:27.948
A, performance. B, talent. C, wellbeing.

79
00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:33.650
The answer is C: wellbeing.

80
00:05:34.817 --> 00:05:36.549
Choose the correct sentence.

81
00:05:36.849 --> 00:05:44.392
A, It is vital that he receives training.. B, It is vital that he receive training.. C, It is vital that he to receive training..

82
00:05:47.933 --> 00:05:50.897
The answer is B: It is vital that he receive training..

83
00:05:52.050 --> 00:05:54.990
According to the reading, people often leave because of…

84
00:05:55.290 --> 00:05:59.733
A, their managers. B, the company logo. C, office furniture.

85
00:06:03.267 --> 00:06:05.858
The answer is A: their managers.

86
00:06:07.067 --> 00:06:10.207
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:13.572
What makes employees want to stay with a company?

88
00:06:30.383 --> 00:06:31.942
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:32.242 --> 00:07:08.106
Employees usually stay when they feel respected, fairly rewarded and able to grow. Salary matters, but research shows that a supportive manager and clear career opportunities are often more important. It is essential that people receive recognition for good work and training for the next step in their careers. For example, a bank that promotes tellers into supervisor roles shows staff they have a future there. In my view, a positive culture is the strongest reason anyone stays.

90
00:07:08.406 --> 00:07:10.313
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:07:11.217 --> 00:07:15.970
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and it is essential that plus subjunctive.

92
00:07:16.270 --> 00:07:19.701
Today's value is respect. Thank the people who help us.

93
00:07:20.001 --> 00:07:22.978
See you in Unit twenty-three. Goodbye!

94
00:07:23.278 --> 00:07:25.849
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

